  "contract": [
    "Workspace clears344 bytes, then creates nine filter records in native order including offset84 before74, nine s16 queues with capacities180 except slot7 at60, and seven float records of20/mode1. Native calls ceil with exact binary64 60.0, then converts the exact result to unsigned60; this caller-specific constant is folded without admitting a generic math replacement.",
    "Pair helper allocates wrapping32-bit (source_count>>1)*8 bytes, then passes only the low8 bits of the half-count to descriptor initialization. Float arguments are ignored. Descriptor writes count byte and coefficient pointer, clears full count*8 bytes, writes state pointer after clearing and returns end pointer. No allocation guards or padding clears invented.",
    "Canonical existing HBA resources are reused. Four getter bodies return corresponding view.words pointers; all64252 graph-resource bytes and80 filter-coefficient bytes match stock spans and remain unchanged. Readonly object/section flags verified; no duplicate resource definition or executable resource is introduced.",
    "477 direct comparisons with independent full workspace, queue/filter, allocation and state-zero oracles execute all440 native instruction bytes. Only malloc is modeled; existing C queues/memory primitives execute. Native exact ceil/conversion inputs are independently observed in the reference execution.",
    "128 full HR constructor/allocator/complete-teardown cases execute actual C workspace, filter helpers, resource getters, queues and heap code. All primary/workspace/filter/graph/queue allocations release back to prior heap top."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Graph constructor internals remain modeled: three graph records preallocated by each real allocator transfer through modeled returns. Provider internal allocations/timing and numerical inference are unproven. Five external system/logging bindings remain in the fixture; normal successful lifecycle calls exercise graph provider only.",
    "Resource pointers are normalized only in comparison output and graph-provider argument traces, never rewritten during execution. Full data equality proves supplied resource contents, not future graph cursor bounds or inference correctness.",
    "First nine workspace allocation failures and positive-size null descriptor states compare logical write faults only. Physical access width/fault behavior, invalid pointers, concurrency, cold FP activation, caller scratch and private frames remain outside proof.",
    "The function-frontier pair-helper size52 overlapped the next admitted version routine at667e4. Fresh control flow establishes30 bytes ending in the tail branch to92848. Only those30 bytes are admitted; the version row is unchanged.",
    "An initial full composition rejected a duplicate coefficient symbol introduced by the first candidate. It was removed in favor of the canonical model-data view; all final corpora, defects and final composition use the canonical resource. The failed report is preserved as evidence, not counted as successful composition.",
    "The887-unit final ld-r composition passes without failures or duplicate strong symbols.876 prior nongenerated source/object pairs unchanged, tested object equals normal object, no new writable state/resource definitions. Five imports removed, application78 to73; boot22.",
    "Generic ceil still retains its existing implementation elsewhere. This known-constant caller no longer requires that path. Final executable linking/startup, hardware delivery, graph construction, numerical inference and boot remain open."
  ],
